The skill makes every inbox message get a reply, because replying was
the only way out of the inbox. So a message that asks nothing, like a
thanks or an applied notice, still drew an acknowledgement. That reply
then sat in the sender's inbox in turn, and the thread never closed.

With the archive in place, those messages can leave the inbox without
adding anything to the list. Anything that asks a question or needs a
decision acknowledged still gets a reply, and in doubt the skill
replies.
